    "geometry": "point",
    "attributes": {
        "name": "string",
        "description": "string",
        "location": "point"
    }
}

# Create a new feature
feature = {
    "geometry": {
        "x": -122.45,
        "y": 37.78,
        "spatialReference": {
            "wkid": 102100
        }
    },
    "attributes": {
        "name": "Golden Gate Bridge",
        "description": "A famous suspension bridge in San Francisco.",
        "location": {
            "x": -122.45,
            "y": 37.78
        }
    }
}

# Add the feature to the feature layer
feature_layer.add_feature(feature)

# Save the feature layer to ArcGIS Online
feature_layer.publish("my_feature_layer")

print("Feature added and published successfully!")
```

In this example, we first connect to an ArcGIS Online account, then create a new feature layer. We define a schema for the feature, create a new feature with a point geometry and attributes, and finally add the feature to the feature layer and publish it to ArcGIS Online. Make sure to replace `"your_username"` and `"your_password"` with your actual ArcGIS Online credentials.

