     user_id: "user_id",
     location: "user_location",
     device_type: "device_type"
   });
   ```

5. **Analyze Data**: Use Firebase Analytics reports to analyze the data. Look for trends, spikes, and anomalies in the read events. This can help you identify the root cause of the high read volume.

6. **Set Up Alerts**: Configure Firebase Performance Monitoring to set up alerts for unusual spikes in read latency or failure rates. This will help you respond quickly to any issues.

7. **Review Code**: Review your code to ensure that you are not unintentionally triggering multiple read operations. Look for loops, recursive calls, or event listeners that might be causing excessive reads.

By following these steps, you can instrument Firebase calls effectively and gain valuable insights into why you have so many reads. This will help you optimize your application and improve performance.
